.TH BOSWAS-COMPAT-MANAGER 1 "October 2026" "boswas-compat-manager 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-compat-manager \- manage Windows applications on Boswas OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-compat-manager
.RB [ \-\-install
.IR file ]
.br
.B boswas-compat-manager
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-compat-manager
is the Boswas OS Compatibility Manager, the desktop application for Windows
applications. It installs, starts, stops, repairs, updates and removes
Windows applications, shows their logs and the permissions they have, and
shows the health of the compatibility runtime and of device management.
.PP
The Compatibility Manager runs as the desktop user and never as root. It
does not run Windows software or any other program itself: every operation
is a request to the user's Boswas session service, which applies the
compatibility catalog, the device policy, the per\-application sandbox and
the AppArmor confinement exactly as
.BR boswas\-winapp (1)
does. Permissions are shown read\-only; they come from the Boswas
compatibility catalog and the device policy and cannot be changed in the
Compatibility Manager.
.PP
Boswas OS runs x86_64 (64\-bit) Windows applications only. A 32\-bit
installer is refused with the message
.RI \(lq "This application requires 32-bit Windows compatibility, which is not supported by Boswas OS." \(rq
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-install " file"
Open the install page and check
.I file
(a Windows program or Windows Installer package). Nothing is installed
before the check result is shown and the installation is confirmed. The
file manager action \(lqInstall with Boswas Compatibility Manager\(rq uses
this option.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/boswas/session.sock
The user's Boswas session service, used for every application operation.
.TP
.I /run/boswas\-agent/agent.sock
The Boswas device agent, used read\-only for the device, Control Plane and
policy status.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window was closed normally; 4 when started as root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas\-winapp (1)
